ng for pAkt in grade III oligodendroglioma. (c)Caspase-3 positive nucleus, GBM. (d) Beclin 1 positive cytoplasmic and nuclearstaining, GBM. (e) PARP1 positive nuclei, GBM. (f) Cleaved-PARP1 positivenucleus, GBM. DAB, 400&#x000d7; .</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="JO2008-219241.003"/></fig><fig id="fig4" position="float"><label>Figure 4</label><caption><p>(a) Western blotting of pAkt expression. Positivebands in a sample of 8 cases. (b) Quantitative analysis of pAkt levels normalized to <italic>&#x003b2;</italic>-actin data.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="JO2008-219241.004"/></fig><table-wrap id="tab1" position="float"><label>Table 1</label><caption><p>Scoring system for evaluation of immunostaining.</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups"><thead><tr><th align="left" rowspan="2" colspan="1">Marker</th><th align="center" colspan="3" rowspan="1">Category</th></tr><tr><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">A</th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">B</th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">C</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">pStat3 and pAkt</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Diffuse, &#x0003c;20%, +   with or without foci</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Diffuse, 20&#x02013;50%, ++   with or without foci</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Diffuse, &#x0003e;50% or &#x0003e;20%, +++with multiple foci</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Ki-67/MIB.1</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x0003c;20%</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">20&#x02013;30%</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x0003e;30%</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">EGFR Amplification</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Non-amplified</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Non-amplified</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">More than 2 copies</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">EGFRwt</td><td a